From 1ab3ad11c688653d7c1e7056a13ec6a86fd8dab1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 08:35:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06858/11362] [outer-loop] ARC sc25 round-4: L5->L6, FULL GAME
 CLEAR

Round-4 codex gpt-5.6-sol attempt on sc25 solved L6, the terminal level of
the whole six-level game. Routes AROUND round-3's southwest-socket trap
entirely: the persistent northern 9/a sprite is not the controllable
player, it's a fixed WIN-CONDITION SILHOUETTE that stays in place after
the first B-cast teleport spawns a movable copy elsewhere. Break both
linked-color boxes (6dd6/6cc6, clearing the east-channel and north-shaft
walls), collect both energy pickups, then B-cast directly from the second
pickup while full-size (not mini -- this is what avoids the southwest
lock) to teleport to the junction, then walk the cleared shaft to overlap
the silhouette. Live win at levels_completed=6 with terminal WIN after 206
calls; fresh-reset reproduce() independently confirmed reached_level=6.

Independently re-verified by the outer loop: 5x fresh env.reset() +
replay, all 5 confirmed level=6, state=GameState.WIN.

Fixed two real bugs surfaced by this replay:
- resolve_replay_plan's sc25 branch was unconditional and always returned
  the 16-label L1-only plan regardless of claimed level (silent bug the
  source agent hit live and worked around); now level-aware via
  SC25_PLANS_BY_LEVEL, with a new >=6 branch for this win.
- label_to_action_data didn't recognize the "wait" label (an explicit
  ACTION5 cast-animation resolve, distinct from "warmup"); aliased both.

reproducible_total_levels 146 -> 147 (13th full game clear).
arc_count_integrity_lint.py exit 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
